    "readingTime": 4,
    "summary": "Ditching crowded Baga beaches for a bicycle ride through the silent river island of Divar in the Mandovi river.",
    "content": "\n        <p>Take a 5-minute free government vehicle ferry from Old Goa or Ribandar across the Mandovi river, and you step back in time 70 years. Divar Island has no commercial resorts, no beach shacks, and no techno clubs.</p>\n        <h3>What to Do in Divar:</h3>\n        <ul>\n          <li><strong>Rent a Cycle:</strong> The island is crisscrossed with smooth tarmac lanes flanked by emerald paddy fields, sleepy fishing sluice gates (<em>Manos</em>), and pastel-painted Portuguese baroque houses with oyster-shell windows.</li>\n          <li><strong>Our Lady of Piety Church:</strong> Perched on the highest hill of the island, offering a 360-degree sunset panorama over Old Goa's Se Cathedral towers.</li>\n          <li><strong>Local Food:</strong> Eat at <em>Rock Inn Bar & Restaurant</em>\u2014a rustic tavern serving fresh crab Xec Xec, Goan poi bread, and homemade cashew feni for under \u20b9400.</li>\n        </ul>\n        "
