    "content": "\n            <p>If you rush through Dzukou Valley in a weekend, you miss its true essence. This is a place that rewards patience, conversations with tea shop owners, and early morning strolls before the day heats up.</p>\n            <h3>Accommodation on a Budget</h3>\n            <p>Skip the commercial booking apps. Walk into the older quarters of Dzukou Valley to find authentic family-run homestays charging between \u20b9800 and \u20b91,500 per night. You get clean bedding, filtered spring water, and real homecooked food made with local seasonal produce.</p>\n            <h3>Getting Around</h3>\n            <ul>\n              <li>Local shared jeeps and state transport buses run reliably between 7:00 AM and 5:00 PM. Fares rarely exceed \u20b950\u2013\u20b9100.</li>\n              <li>Carry enough liquid cash in small denominations (\u20b950, \u20b9100, \u20b9200); ATMs here often run out of cash during busy weekends.</li>\n            </ul>\n            <p><strong>Local Respect:</strong> Always take your plastic waste back with you to the nearest district center. Leave nothing behind but footprints.</p>\n            "
